+The first repaired schedule (v3.1) still correlated canonical palettes with two colors and extended palettes with three; a test-first self-review exposed that shortcut. Version 3.2 uses four orthogonal profiles: center/canonical/2, center/extended/3, off-center/canonical/3, off-center/extended/2. Any three demonstrations retain an off-center, extended-palette, and three-color witness.
+
+Changing the version altered keyed RNG samples and exposed morphology drift: the old equal scattered/connected/snake cycle yielded a nonzero-component median of 1 against canonical 6 in the exact regression. The final layout cycle is four scattered, one connected, one snake; final shared distribution gate passes while connected examples remain represented.
